{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"TailwindLabs.TailwindCSS","latestVersion":"4.3.5","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"Tailwind Labs","copyright":"Copyright (c) Tailwind Labs, Inc.","description":"Rapidly build modern websites without ever leaving your HTML.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation"}],"license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/blob/master/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"Tailwind Labs","copyright":"Copyright (c) Tailwind Labs, Inc.","description":"Rapidly build modern websites without ever leaving your HTML.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation"}],"license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/blob/master/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Tailwind CSS works by scanning all of your HTML files, JavaScript components, and any other templates for class names, generating the corresponding styles and then writing them to a static CSS file.\nIt's fast, flexible, and reliable — with zero-runtime.","name":"Tailwind CSS","packageUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","publisher":"Tailwind Labs","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/issues","publisherUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","releaseNotes":"Fixed\n- Canonicalization: improve performance in projects with many functional variant values (e.g. a matchVariant plugin with thousands of values) (#20663)\n- Don't crash or create a fallback with the wrong color for a color-mix(…) without a color interpolation method (e.g. color-mix(var(--color-red-500)) or color-mix(currentcolor 50%, transparent)) (#20658, #20666)\n- Ensure @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi loads instead of hanging forever (e.g. with NAPI_RS_FORCE_WASI=error or in WebContainers) (#20667)\n- Remove as: '*.css' from the @tailwindcss/turbopack setup in its README, because it breaks CSS modules (#20660)\n- Ignore <!-- and --> between top-level rules in CSS instead of throwing or swallowing the next rule (e.g. a { color: red } --> b { color: blue }) (#20665)\n- Ensure @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi detects changed and new source files after the first scan (e.g. in WebContainers) (#20487)\n- Prevent type errors with skipLibCheck: false caused by imports of unshipped modules in the @tailwindcss/node type declarations (#20632)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/releases/tag/v4.3.5","tags":["css"]},"zh-CN":{"author":"Tailwind Labs","copyright":"Copyright (c) Tailwind Labs, Inc.","description":"无需脱离 HTML 就能快速构建现代网站","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"文档","DocumentUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation"}],"license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/blob/master/LICENSE","locale":"zh-CN","longDescription":"Tailwind CSS 的工作原理是扫描您所有的 HTML 文件、JavaScript 组件以及其它任何模板的类名，生成相应的样式，然后将其写入一个静态 CSS 文件中。快速、灵活、可靠，并且零等待。","name":"Tailwind CSS","packageUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","publisher":"Tailwind Labs","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/issues","publisherUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/releases/tag/v4.3.5","tags":["css"]}},"longDescription":"Tailwind CSS works by scanning all of your HTML files, JavaScript components, and any other templates for class names, generating the corresponding styles and then writing them to a static CSS file.\nIt's fast, flexible, and reliable — with zero-runtime.","name":"Tailwind CSS","packageUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","publisher":"Tailwind Labs","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/issues","publisherUrl":"https://tailwindcss.com","releaseNotes":"Fixed\n- Canonicalization: improve performance in projects with many functional variant values (e.g. a matchVariant plugin with thousands of values) (#20663)\n- Don't crash or create a fallback with the wrong color for a color-mix(…) without a color interpolation method (e.g. color-mix(var(--color-red-500)) or color-mix(currentcolor 50%, transparent)) (#20658, #20666)\n- Ensure @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi loads instead of hanging forever (e.g. with NAPI_RS_FORCE_WASI=error or in WebContainers) (#20667)\n- Remove as: '*.css' from the @tailwindcss/turbopack setup in its README, because it breaks CSS modules (#20660)\n- Ignore <!-- and --> between top-level rules in CSS instead of throwing or swallowing the next rule (e.g. a { color: red } --> b { color: blue }) (#20665)\n- Ensure @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi detects changed and new source files after the first scan (e.g. in WebContainers) (#20487)\n- Prevent type errors with skipLibCheck: false caused by imports of unshipped modules in the @tailwindcss/node type declarations (#20632)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/releases/tag/v4.3.5","tags":["css"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.5/app.json","detailSha256":"846ecd54374d53c5b267f9400e7deeaebcf0a031c8c8c61fb4a3ae79bae50fe2","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"4.3.5"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.4/app.json","detailSha256":"7e1c19573b7466e27e1d5bf5370122713e31c6c91f9762a21dc0fd2664685008","releaseDate":"2026-11-02","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.3.4"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.3/app.json","detailSha256":"608eddda130e7e4f7f60f69820185083fa03b13ebeb20cff19c1dc4b3cd2bcb3","releaseDate":"2026-07-16","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.3.3"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.2/app.json","detailSha256":"b05dc72d166ad1b29367d01a349d85e406bcceeca6aa067b24aaf737438eb8d8","releaseDate":"2026-06-29","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.3.2"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.1/app.json","detailSha256":"3d5f6cf92fd